# curl|sh bootstrap for `dotfiles-init` — lives at repo root so
# `curl … | bash` is a simple one-liner, but it's tooling-for-init,
# not something that should land in $HOME/bootstrap.sh.
# See scripts/init/README.md.
bootstrap.sh

*.txt   # ignore *.txt in the target directory
*/*.txt # ignore *.txt in subdirectories of the target directory
        # but not in subdirectories of subdirectories;
        # so a/b/c.txt would *not* be ignored

*/*.org# # Ignore org-mode backup files that end with `#`

backups/   # ignore the backups folder, but not its contents
backups/** # ignore the contents of backups folder but not the folder itself

docs/** # ignore everything in docs/ and its subdirectories

backlog/** # ignore long-term backlog research (repo metadata, not user config)

pitfalls/** # ignore past-pitfalls knowledge base (repo metadata, not user config)

# Agent skills installed via `npx skills`.
#
# Project-scope (chezmoi repo's own .agents/skills/ + .claude/skills/ + skills-lock.json):
#   These exist purely so the chezmoi repo itself can use project-scope skills
#   while you edit it.  They MUST NOT deploy — global install at ~/.agents/skills/
#   already covers every machine.  Auto-restored on `chezmoi apply` by
#   .chezmoiscripts/repo/run_onchange_after_45_bootstrap_skills.sh.tmpl when source dir == repo;
#   manual fallback: `just bootstrap-skills` (or `npx skills experimental_install`).
#
# Global-scope (~/.agents/.skill-lock.json + ~/.agents/skills/):
#   The lock file IS chezmoi-managed via dot_agents/modify_dot_skill-lock.json.tmpl
#   (merger script, see docs/tools/agent-skills.md).  The skills/ folder under
#   it is owned by the npx skills CLI and re-populated by
#   run_onchange_after_install_global_skills.sh.tmpl whenever the lock changes,
#   so we do NOT want chezmoi to manage skills/ contents directly.
.agents/skills
.agents/skills/**
.claude/skills
.claude/skills/**
skills-lock.json

scripts/**

